import json

def add_v19(d,P,new_page,para,table,picture,link,is_glasses):
 O=P/'engineering-v19-results';s=json.loads((O/'handoff_summary.json').read_text());r=json.loads((O/'test_register.json').read_text());j=json.loads((O/'joint_verification.json').read_text())
 new_page(d,'V19 Prototype assembly and next decision')
 para(d,'Project status: V19 six size assembly prototype with conditional joint calculations and V10 native archives.')
 para(d,'V19 keeps the six adjustable sizes and changes the hinge hardware. Each hinge now has two nested disc springs, a longer proposed pin and a second nut. The final local STEP assemblies contain 42 solids each. The current geometry is a prototype for review. Native editable Fusion archives remain V10. No physical material, sound, comfort or durability test has been performed.')
 picture(d,'V19_hero','Actual final V19 STEP surfaces for child large and adult small. Colours identify parts and do not select materials.',5.9)
 para(d,'The exact helical thread experiment was rejected. A validity check initially passed, but the pin contained two disconnected solids and the Boolean operation lost its core. We kept the failed trial and excluded it from the final assemblies. Current fasteners use cosmetic thread envelopes and proposed M4 x 0.7 drawing callouts. Thread strength, drive, runout, tolerances and effective locking still need supplier and bench review.')
 if is_glasses:para(d,'This hinge change belongs to the standalone defender. The Sony WH CH720N replacement pad is unchanged. It has no model-specific fit or sound pass. The shared material and measurement findings below apply to both routes.')
 new_page(d,'V19 Folding and holding tradeoff')
 picture(d,'V19_folded_CAD','Saved V19 retracted and folded surfaces. Sampled collision checks do not establish continuous motion clearance, wrench access or handling strength.',5.4)
 para(d,'The revised geometry has '+str(r['motion_sample_count'])+' recorded rigid pose samples and '+str(r['stop_query_count'])+' outward stop queries across six sizes. The 18 saved wear, retracted and folded pose exports were separately reimported and checked. These are geometry checks, not wear or fatigue tests.')
 table(d,['Prototype hinge detail','Nominal proposal'],[['Plain pin diameter and pivot bore','4 mm and 4.3 mm'],['Child pin underhead and plain shoulder','45 mm and 37 mm'],['Adult pin underhead and plain shoulder','65 mm and 57 mm'],['Thread callout and length','M4 x 0.7 for 8 mm; cosmetic CAD thread'],['Primary nut and jam nut heights','3.2 mm and 2.2 mm; both 7 mm across flats'],['Nominal pin tip beyond both nuts','1.9375 mm before tolerances'],['Disc pair reference height and force','0.6625 mm and 236 N at catalogue reference shortening']],[3.0,3.9])
 para(d,'Two nuts are proposed for countertightening while holding the primary nut. We still need to prove access with real tools and remeasure hinge torque after locking. The disc reference position is not a measured assembly setting. A nominal radial clearance budget leaves 0.06 mm after chosen diameter, axis and growth errors. Supplier capability has not been demonstrated.')
 new_page(d,'V19 Retention and folding effort')
 picture(d,'V19_retention','Equivalent static moment comparison. The torque lines are chosen targets, not measured hinge properties. This is not a drop or shake simulation.',5.8)
 para(d,'The proposed target rises from 80 to 160 Nmm, with a chosen 128 to 192 Nmm comparison window. This doubles the earlier target and gives a worst assumed equivalent static threshold of about '+f"{s['minimum_static_equivalent_g_threshold']:.2f}"+' g. All '+str(s['static_comparison_count']//4)+' assumed mass cases fall below the proposed minimum at 2 g. At higher acceleration some exceed it. The calculation inherits V18 moving cup and fork masses, which are unchanged; it does not predict impact dynamics.')
 para(d,'At a 65 mm grip lever, that window corresponds to about 1.97 to 2.95 N folding force. More holding torque also means harder folding. We have no sensory acceptance limit for this force. Measure breakaway and running torque in both directions, then check drift after bedding, humidity, temperature and cycling. The higher target does not prove that the hinge will stay closed in a bag or stay comfortable to use.')
 para(d,'SCHNORR describes parallel stacks as adding force at the same deflection. Our two-disc reference is based on its 000600B data. Real spring variation, friction, settling and plastic creep can change the assembly. Set torque by measurement, not by copying a nut position from the drawing.')
 link(d,'SCHNORR disc spring stacking guidance','https://schnorr.com/our-products/disc-springs/')
 new_page(d,'V19 Coupled joint calculation and limits')
 picture(d,'V19_joint_refinement','Solved displacement at the chosen outward 2 N fixture load. This model is a numerical development study; the final refinement result and gate are stated below.',5.8)
 solved=sum(c.get('converged',True) for c in r['joint_cases']);failed=len(r['joint_cases'])-solved
 para(d,'We added a three dimensional calculation with flexible fork and tongue, one-way stop contact, washer contact and friction-limited tangential springs. There are '+str(len(r['joint_cases']))+' current cases: '+str(solved)+' converged and '+str(failed)+' did not converge. These counts describe numerical solves, not physical passes. Earlier low-preload low-friction runs reached the 80 iteration limit. Their failed records are retained alongside the later retry results. More iterations can fix an iteration-limit failure without proving physical holding or strength.')
 para(d,'The model applies a prescribed preload and uses an ideal distributing pivot connector. It does not resolve real pin bearing clearance, bolt bending, thread load, disc spring deformation, guide contact or the full worn headset. The reference elastic modulus is 3500 MPa for TECAMID 66 natural and Poisson ratio 0.35 is assumed. This is a reference material calculation, not a qualified part grade or a prediction of long-term performance.')
 new_page(d,'V19 Joint convergence and scope')
 comps=j['mesh_comparisons'];table(d,['Family and mesh change','Displacement change','Chosen 5 percent comparison'],[[c['size'].replace('_',' ')+' '+str(c['from_h'])+' to '+str(c['to_h'])+' mm',f"{c['displacement_change_percent']:.1f}%",'Pass' if c['chosen_5_percent_gate_pass'] else 'Fail'] for c in comps],[3.2,1.5,2.2])
 para(d,'Reassembled equations, saved array comparisons, force balance, source hashes and a constant-strain control pass for '+str(len(j['array_audits']))+' saved solves. These checks find algebra and file problems; they do not validate the physical model. Mesh results that miss the chosen limit are not hidden or promoted to a strength pass. There is no complete joint or whole-headset strength qualification.')
 para(d,'The finest requested mesh in this run is 0.8 mm, with a chosen limit of 30000 nodes. A memory snapshot during the adult refinement showed about 1.3 GB free on the 16 GB laptop. This is a bounded study limit, not a proven hardware maximum. Further joint refinement or a different solver remains computer work if the numerical limit is not met; it is not being relabelled as completed physical testing.')
 new_page(d,'V19 Material finding and prototype records')
 para(d,'We checked additional published foam reference points rather than inventing a winning new material. PORON 4701-30 lists typical 25 percent compression pressures of 21, 35 and 62 kPa for its three density options. Under ideal uniform compression across our full annulus, those points imply the forces below. They do not provide a full loading and unloading curve for our pad.')
 table(d,['Reference density','Child annulus force at 25 percent','Adult annulus force at 25 percent'],[[str(density)+' kg per cubic metre',f"{next(x for x in s['foam_reference_points'] if x['family']=='child' and x['density_kg_m3']==density)['ideal_uniform_25_percent_force_N']:.1f} N",f"{next(x for x in s['foam_reference_points'] if x['family']=='adult' and x['density_kg_m3']==density)['ideal_uniform_25_percent_force_N']:.1f} N"] for density in [240,320,400]],[2.0,2.45,2.45])
 para(d,'These ideal forces are much greater than the earlier 2 N per cup screening load. A material called very soft may still be unsuitable as a whole cushion at the required compression. This is a reason to request real samples and curves, not a comfort rejection based on one point. Supplier sheet thicknesses also do not automatically provide our full pad depth. We have not selected this foam or demonstrated its cost in India.')
 link(d,'Rogers PORON 4701 30 data sheet','https://rogerscorp.com/-/media/project/rogerscorp/documents/elastomeric-material-solutions/poron/english/data-sheets/17-006-poron-4701-30-very-soft.pdf')
 para(d,'The handoff folder now contains CAD part envelopes, key dimensions, a nominal dimension-review PDF, assembly notes, blank material and test records, a Sony measurement form, a supplier quotation form and a measured-input readiness checker. No supplier was contacted and no quotation was obtained. The PDF is a prototype dimensional review, not a complete production drawing. Inputs remain blank because we have not measured a real sample.')
 new_page(d,'V19 What we can conclude now')
 if is_glasses:picture(d,'V19_Sony_measurements','Measurement guide only. The pictured oval is illustrative and is not the Sony mounting shape.',3.6)
 table(d,['Workstream','Current decision'],[['Six sizes adjustment folding and saved STEP poses','Recorded finite geometry checks completed'],['Component band tongue and fork fixtures','Earlier conditional numerical checks retained'],['Coupled 3D joint','Development model; see failed solves and refinement limits'],['Full worn foam cover and skin contact','Not calibrated or validated'],['Real acoustics heat durability and sensory acceptance','No product validation pass'],['Sony WH CH720N compatible carrier','Original pad and mount measurements still required'],['Native editable Fusion update','Current native archives V10; V19 is local STEP'],['Production tolerances final materials and cost','Supplier and sample evidence still required']],[3.1,3.8])
 para(d,'The computer package is a traceable prototype handoff. It is not evidence that every possible computer analysis is finished. A full validated worn model, exact Sony fit and production release are still open. More arbitrary simulation inputs cannot prove comfort, sound reduction, zero leakage, sensory acceptance or that we outperform market headphones. Earlier reduced contact, acoustic and thermal models remain exploratory.')
 para(d,'Next collect actual foam and cover curves, hinge torque and headband force, plus the original Sony mounting dimensions. Build a bench hinge and pad sample, compare measurements with the models, then revise the CAD and make a complete fixture prototype. Voluntary wearer feedback is needed before any claim about autistic users. Both living reports must continue to update together when real measurements or new revisions arrive.')
